# 62-vu1-gs-cost-diag: measurement only. GOW_VU1_COST=1 / GOW_GS_COST=1 split the time of the two hot threads; both
# off by default, and while off the cost is a static branch test per run / per block / per primitive (no rdtsc).
#
# VU1 (ps2_vu1_native.h, ps2_vu1_native.inl, ps2_vu1_core.cpp): [vu1-cost], every 5 s: run_ms (the same wall time
# [gow-perf] reports as vu_ms), runs (one VU1 program run each), entries, blocks, pairs; the share of run_ms spent
# inside the generated block functions (1/8 of the calls sampled, rdtsc overhead subtracted, scaled back), in the
# native dispatch loop, in the per-run entry (flag import, commit of the exact engine's results) and exit
# (syncInflight/exportFlags), and in the XGKICK tag walk (xgkicks, KB, and how much of that is submitGifPacket).
#
# GS (gs_hw_backend.cpp): [gs-cost] (submits/s, ns per primitive, the sameState comparison, state flushes, batches and
# us per batch, and the per-batch split pre/uni/tex/vert/draw/post) and [gs-cost2] (the sub-parts pre_tgt, pre_fbo,
# pre_state, tex_lookup, tex_bind, tex_scan, tex_resolve, tex_pack). Both lines print the thread they are reported from.
#
# Measured (i3-4170 + HD 4400, Asia disc, fast boot attract/replay demo, 70 s, 5 s windows, 0.5x internal, VU1 x64 fast):
#   VU1  run_ms 4.32-4.63 s, 105k-124k runs, 31-37 M blocks, 246-287 M pairs -> 143-170 ns per block, 18.4-21.8 ns per
#        pair. blockcode ~100 % of run_ms after the rdtsc correction (the raw line prints 112-124 %), dispatch 0.0 %,
#        entry 1.3-1.7 %, exit 0.5-1.2 %: the VU1 wall time is the generated block bodies, there is no dispatch layer
#        left to cut. xgkicks 211k-246k per 5 s (298-348 MB), xgkick_ms 432-601 (8-11 % of the block time, 26-45 %
#        in the cutscene windows), and 96-98 % of that is submitGifPacket: the GS frontend runs on this worker thread.
#   GS   submit 259-285 ns per primitive (253-500 ns in the cutscene windows, where draws go 4-8 M per 5 s), of which
#        sameState is 39-44 ns; drawOne 90-98 us per batch over 13k-22k batches, split pre 21 % (pre_fbo 134-444 ms/5 s,
#        pre_tgt 52-117 ms), uni 4-5 %, tex 42-47 % (tex_resolve 430-472 ms from ~850 real decodes at ~500 us each;
#        tex_scan 3 ms, tex_pack 1 ms, tex_bind 68-118 ms), vert 8-10 %, draw 19-22 %, post 1 %.
#
# Measured and rejected while writing this patch (the notes in the code say why): the binary search over uploadLog
# (tex_scan was already only 3 ms per 5 s), and handing PATH1 XGKICK packets to the GS worker job FIFO (the VU1 and the
# GS frontend already share that worker thread, so the handoff never engaged and the numbers did not move: vu_ms
# 4490-4649 with it, 4152-4659 without).
